# Agent Coordination

Spec: AgentCoordination
Purpose:
   Define how agents coordinate: handoff protocols, context passing,
   conflict resolution, and the agent activity log.

Owns: agents/coordination.sdd

CoordinationModel:
   principle: agents coordinate via shared state, not direct messages
   anti_pattern: Agent A says "I changed payment" → Agent B says "OK"
   preferred: STATE records the change; Agent B reads state

AgentHandoff:
   mechanism: HANDFOFF-NN
   fields:
     done: [completed work]
     pending: [remaining work]
     important: [critical notes]
     risk: risk level
     next: [next steps]

   ContextHandoff:
     @handoff.H22
     task: T2041
     state: implementation-complete
     references: [DEC-88, ARCH-12, SKILL-REFUND-3]
     proof: unit-pass
     unknown: [integration behavior]

   TestHandoff:
     @handoff.H22
     subtask_id: ST-XXX
     test_level: SUBTASK|MODULE|SYSTEM
     test_results: { passed, failed, coverage }
     artifacts: [test_report.xml, coverage.json]
     defects: [DEF-XXX]
     next_actions: [FIX|REGRESSION|DONE]

   UnknownTracking:
     principle: unknown information must be tracked
     @unknown.U44
     question: "Should refund retry happen before or after transaction commit?"
     context: payment/refund
     status: unresolved

     flow: unknown → research_task → reference → answer → decision

TestResultAggregation:
   principle: test results flow upward through the hierarchy
   SUBTOTAL: implementer agent → SUBTASK level results
   MODULE: QA agent aggregates SUBTASK → MODULE level
   SYSTEM: Business agent aggregates MODULE → SYSTEM level
   rule: ALL test levels MUST pass before advancing

DefectRouting:
   principle: defects routed to responsible agent based on attribution
   SUBTASK defect: assigned to implementer agent
   MODULE defect: assigned to QA agent + implementer
   SYSTEM defect: assigned to Business agent + QA + implementer
   rule: DEFECT attribution MUST include agent_id and mu_id

ConflictResolution:
   detection: two agents produce conflicting decisions
   example:
     Agent A: Redis
     Agent B: PostgreSQL
   system_response:
     CONFLICT → DECISION_REQUIRED
   record:
     @conflict.C44
     subject: caching strategy
     position_a: Redis
     position_b: PostgreSQL
     evidence_a: [...]
     evidence_b: [...]
     resolution: pending

   rule: AI must NOT silently pick one side; conflict must be explicit

ConflictRecord:
   flow:
     CONFLICT
      ↓
     DECISION_REQUIRED
      ↓
     Architect agent resolves
      ↓
     @decision.D91 created
      ↓
     conflict: RESOLVED

AgentActivityLog:
   purpose: engineering timeline for later audit
   entries:
     - timestamp, agent_id, action, task_id, outcome
   format: structured, append-only

State: +
   (Added TestResultAggregation and DefectRouting sections)
   (Test results flow: SUBTASK → MODULE → SYSTEM)
   (Defects routed to responsible agents by attribution)
